(begin-tx "LQD-03pre — the pause really is a precondition, not decoration")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [LQD-03pre · 01 · refused, and now it says why] ---")
;;TWO DEFECTS IN ONE LINE, BOTH FIXED 2026-09-12 (owner-authorised). The pause precondition always
;;worked -- migration IS refused while GAP is off -- but the caller learned nothing from it.
;;
;;  1] The message was wrapped in a ONE-ARGUMENT `(format …)`. Pact's format takes a template AND an
;;     argument list, so building the message was itself an arity error: it resolved to a closure and
;;     the transaction died with "Expected Pact Value, got closure or table reference". The guard's
;;     own words never reached the operator. Four more sites shared the shape; all five are repaired
;;     and `python3 tools/_conformance.py --rule format-no-arglist` now keeps it at 0.
;;
;;  2] The sentence was BACKWARDS. `enforce gap` requires the pause to be ON, and the message said
;;     "offline". Five sites elsewhere (TS01-C2:197, C3:158, C4:145, TS01-P:111, TS02-CPAD:110) all
;;     use "online" to mean the pause is on, so the convention was unambiguous and this line was the
;;     odd one out. Now "online".
;;
;;Defect 1 HID defect 2: a message that never renders cannot be noticed to be wrong. That is the
;;general hazard with message-construction bugs, and the reason this assertion now pins the exact
;;sentence rather than just "it was refused".
(env-data { "LQD_PRE_KS": { "keys": ["PK_AncientHodler"], "pred": "keys-all" } })
;;==== LQD-03pre — the pause really is a precondition, not decoration · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== =
(print "--- [LQD-03pre — the pause really is a precondition, not decoration · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
;;==== LQD-03pre — the pause really is a precondition, not decoration · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [LQD-03pre — the pause really is a precondition, not decoration · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
        (ref-TS01-A:module{TalosStageOne_AdminV2} TS01-A)
        (ref-coin:module{stoa-ns.fungible-v1} coin)
        (lq-stoa:string "c:ZNfuj3iZI83n7MUSKGuoXoSxFg1cyMxCzB3szUHVvrI")
    )
    (let ((tgt:string (create-principal (read-keyset "LQD_PRE_KS"))))
        (ref-coin::create-account tgt (read-keyset "LQD_PRE_KS"))
        (let ((e0:decimal (ref-coin::get-balance lq-stoa)))
            (map print
                [
                    (expect "<<LQD-03pre>> GAP is OFF" false (ref-DALOS::UR_GAP))
                    (expect-failure "<<LQD-03pre>> migration is refused while the pause is off, and says so"
                        "Migration can only be executed when Global Administrative Pause is online"
                        (ref-TS01-A::LIQUID|A_MigrateLiquidFunds KST.ANHD tgt))
                    (expect "<<LQD-03pre>> and the escrow is untouched by the refusal"
                        e0 (ref-coin::get-balance lq-stoa))
                ]
            )
        )
    )
    ""
)
(print "===^^^===")
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "LQD-03 — LIQUID|A_MigrateLiquidFunds sweeps the escrow (never exercised before)")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [LQD-03 · 01 · migrate the wrapping escrow] ---")
;; The twin of DALOS|A_MigrateLiquidFunds, and the one the ledger only ever "covered" from raw
;; source text. It sweeps the ENTIRE native-STOA balance of the LIQUID escrow to an arbitrary
;; target so funds can follow a namespace migration.
;;
;; Deliberately the LAST test in this file: it breaks the module's central invariant on purpose.
;; Unlike the DALOS gas station, this account BACKS circulating wrapped STOA 1:1 -- so a
;; migration leaves wrapped tokens outstanding against an empty escrow until the operator
;; re-funds the target. That is the property worth pinning, because it is the reason this op is
;; admin-only and pause-gated rather than a routine treasury move.
;;
;; Precondition. Its message USED to be stated backwards (same defect as the DALOS twin):
;;   (enforce gap "Migration can only be executed when Global Administrative Pause is offline")
;; `enforce gap` passes when gap is TRUE, i.e. when the pause is ONLINE, so the text told an
;; operator to do the opposite of what the guard wanted. Requiring GAP ON was always correct --
;; it freezes the chain for the window in which the escrow is empty. FIXED 2026-09-14 (one word);
;; the wording is pinned by modules/DALOS-ADMIN.repl <<DALOS-ADMIN-03b>>.
(env-data
    ;;A DIFFERENT keyset from LQD-03pre's on purpose: create-principal is deterministic, so the
    ;;same keyset yields the same account and coin.create-account would abort on the second
    ;;insert. GOV|MIGRATE also requires the target to be EMPTY, which a fresh principal is.
    { "LQD_MIGRATE_KS": { "keys": ["PK_Emma"], "pred": "keys-all" } }
)
;;==== LQD-03 — LIQUID|A_MigrateLiquidFunds sweeps the escrow (never exercised before) · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== 
(print "--- [LQD-03 — LIQUID|A_MigrateLiquidFunds sweeps the escrow (never exercised before) · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
;;==== LQD-03 — LIQUID|A_MigrateLiquidFunds sweeps the escrow (never exercised before) · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [LQD-03 — LIQUID|A_MigrateLiquidFunds sweeps the escrow (never exercised before) · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (ref-DALOS:module{OuronetDalosV2} DALOS)
        (ref-DPTF:module{DemiourgosPactTrueFungibleV2} DPTF)
        (ref-TS01-A:module{TalosStageOne_AdminV2} TS01-A)
        (ref-coin:module{stoa-ns.fungible-v1} coin)
        (lq-stoa:string "c:ZNfuj3iZI83n7MUSKGuoXoSxFg1cyMxCzB3szUHVvrI")
    )
    (let
        (
            (target:string (create-principal (read-keyset "LQD_MIGRATE_KS")))
        )
        (ref-coin::create-account target (read-keyset "LQD_MIGRATE_KS"))
        (let
            (
                (escrow0:decimal (ref-coin::get-balance lq-stoa))
                (wrapped0:decimal (ref-DPTF::UR_Supply (ref-DALOS::UR_WrappedStoaID)))
            )
            (map print
                [
                    (expect "<<LQD-03>> the escrow holds the STOA backing the wrapped supply"
                        true (> escrow0 0.0))
                    ;; The escrow is FULLY backing, and here slightly OVER-collateralised: it
                    ;; holds exactly 1.0 native STOA more than the wrapped supply, a surplus
                    ;; present from the boot chain and untouched by wrap/unwrap (both move the
                    ;; two sides by the same amount). So the invariant that actually holds is
                    ;; ">= ", not "= ". Asserting equality here would encode a model the chain
                    ;; does not follow; asserting the surplus EXACTLY is what makes a future
                    ;; leak -- in either direction -- fail this test.
                    (expect "<<LQD-03>> INVARIANT: the escrow fully backs the wrapped supply"
                        true (>= escrow0 wrapped0))
                    (expect "<<LQD-03>> ...with a 1.0 surplus carried over from the boot chain"
                        1.0 (- escrow0 wrapped0))
                    (expect "<<LQD-03>> GAP is OFF before we arm the migration" false (ref-DALOS::UR_GAP))
                ]
            )
            ;;PRECONDITION: arm the pause. GOV|MIGRATE enforces GAP is ON (its message says the
            ;;opposite -- see the header note and DALOS-ADMIN-03b, which pins the same defect).
            (ref-TS01-A::DALOS|A_ToggleGAP KST.ANHD true)
            (let ((moved:decimal (ref-TS01-A::LIQUID|A_MigrateLiquidFunds KST.ANHD target)))
                (map print
                    [
                        ;;The return value is the operator's receipt: it must be the PRE-balance,
                        ;;not a post-read (always 0.0, and identical on a partial transfer).
                        (expect "<<LQD-03>> the op returns the amount moved"
                            escrow0 moved)
                        (expect "<<LQD-03>> the escrow is swept to exactly zero"
                            0.0 (ref-coin::get-balance lq-stoa))
                        (expect "<<LQD-03>> the target received the full balance"
                            escrow0 (ref-coin::get-balance target))
                        ;;CONSERVATION of native STOA -- nothing minted or burned, only moved.
                        (expect "<<LQD-03>> native STOA is conserved across the migration"
                            escrow0 (+ (ref-coin::get-balance lq-stoa) (ref-coin::get-balance target)))
                        ;;...and the invariant the module exists to hold is now BROKEN, by design.
                        (expect "<<LQD-03>> wrapped STOA still circulates after the sweep"
                            wrapped0 (ref-DPTF::UR_Supply (ref-DALOS::UR_WrappedStoaID)))
                        (expect "<<LQD-03>> so the 1:1 backing is deliberately left broken"
                            true (> (ref-DPTF::UR_Supply (ref-DALOS::UR_WrappedStoaID))
                                    (ref-coin::get-balance lq-stoa)))
                    ]
                )
                ""
            )
        )
    )
)
(print "===^^^===")
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
